<p>An annotation is a clickable rectangle laid over a page, and <code>Page</code> places one with <code>addUrl()</code> or
<code>addLink()</code> the same way <code>addImage()</code> places an image. Both annotation types share the same border,
radius and dash settings, covered once in <a href="#border-appearance">Border Appearance</a> rather than twice.</p>
<h2 id="linking-to-a-url">Linking to a URL<a class="anchor" href="#linking-to-a-url" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>Annotation\Url</code> takes a width, a height and a destination URL, in that order:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Annotation\Url</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$page</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>);
<span class="text-var">$url</span>  = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Url</span>(<span class="text-num">120</span>, <span class="text-num">20</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;https://example.com/report&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$page</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addUrl</span>(<span class="text-var">$url</span>, <span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">72</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">700</span>);

<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">writeToFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>(<span class="text-var">$page</span>), <span class="text-type">filename</span>: <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>addUrl($url, $x, $y)</code> places the rectangle's bottom left corner at <code>$x, $y</code>; both default to <code>0</code>.
The compiled annotation dictionary carries the URL exactly as passed:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">TEXT</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code>/Type /Annot
/Subtype /Link
/Rect [72 700 192 720]
/Border [0 0 0]
/A &lt;&lt;/S /URI /URI (https://example.com/report)&gt;&gt;
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>setUrl()</code> and <code>getUrl()</code> change and read the destination after construction.</p>
<p><code>addUrl()</code> returns the page, so a page carries as many URL links as it needs, each added in the same
chain:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Annotation\Url</span>;

<span class="text-var">$page</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>);
<span class="text-var">$page</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addUrl</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Url</span>(<span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-num">20</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;https://example.com/docs&#039;</span>), <span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">72</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">700</span>)
     -&gt;<span class="text-fn">addUrl</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Url</span>(<span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-num">20</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;https://example.com/support&#039;</span>), <span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">72</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">660</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="linking-within-the-document">Linking Within the Document<a class="anchor" href="#linking-within-the-document" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>Annotation\Link</code> takes a width, a height and an <code>$xTarget, $yTarget</code> pair — the point on the
destination page the reader lands on:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Annotation\Link</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$page1</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>);
<span class="text-var">$page2</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>);

<span class="text-var">$link</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Link</span>(<span class="text-num">120</span>, <span class="text-num">20</span>, <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-num">400</span>);
<span class="text-var">$link</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setPageTarget</span>(<span class="text-num">2</span>);
<span class="text-var">$page1</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addLink</span>(<span class="text-var">$link</span>, <span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">72</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">660</span>);

<span class="text-var">$doc</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>();
<span class="text-var">$doc</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addPage</span>(<span class="text-var">$page1</span>);
<span class="text-var">$doc</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addPage</span>(<span class="text-var">$page2</span>);

<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">writeToFile</span>(<span class="text-var">$doc</span>, <span class="text-type">filename</span>: <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/linked.pdf&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>setPageTarget()</code> takes the destination page's 1-based position in the document — <code>2</code> here means the
second page added, regardless of that page's own index. Reading the compiled annotation back confirms
it: the link sits in page one's <code>/Annots</code> array, and its <code>/Dest</code> entry points at page two's own
object, not page one's:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">TEXT</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code>/Dest [5 0 R /XYZ 100 400 0]
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Leave <code>setPageTarget()</code> uncalled and the link targets the page it's added to — the same document
without the <code>setPageTarget(2)</code> line points <code>/Dest</code> at page one's own object instead, turning the
link into an in-page jump.</p>
<p><code>setXTarget()</code> and <code>setYTarget()</code> set the point the destination page scrolls to, matching the
constructor's third and fourth arguments. <code>setZTarget()</code> sets the destination zoom level and
defaults to <code>0</code>, which under the PDF <code>/XYZ</code> format means &quot;leave the reader's current zoom
unchanged&quot; rather than setting a zoom of zero:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Annotation\Link</span>;

<span class="text-var">$link</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Link</span>(<span class="text-num">120</span>, <span class="text-num">20</span>, <span class="text-num">100</span>, <span class="text-num">400</span>);
<span class="text-var">$link</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setZTarget</span>(<span class="text-num">1.5</span>);
<span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$link</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getZTarget</span>(); <span class="text-comment">// 1.5</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>getXTarget()</code>, <code>getYTarget()</code>, <code>getZTarget()</code> and <code>getPageTarget()</code> read the four values back. A
table of contents page is the usual home for several <code>Link</code> annotations at once, one per entry,
each with its own <code>setPageTarget()</code> pointing further into the document.</p>
<h2 id="sizing-the-clickable-area">Sizing the Clickable Area<a class="anchor" href="#sizing-the-clickable-area" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>The width and height passed to <code>Annotation\Url</code> or <code>Annotation\Link</code>'s constructor set the clickable
rectangle's size, and <code>setWidth()</code> / <code>setHeight()</code> change it afterward — both are inherited from
<code>AbstractAnnotation</code>, so they work identically on either annotation type:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Annotation\Url</span>;

<span class="text-var">$url</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Url</span>(<span class="text-num">120</span>, <span class="text-num">20</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;https://example.com/report&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$url</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setWidth</span>(<span class="text-num">200</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setHeight</span>(<span class="text-num">30</span>);
<span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$url</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getWidth</span>() . <span class="text-str">&#039; x &#039;</span> . <span class="text-var">$url</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getHeight</span>(); <span class="text-comment">// 200 x 30</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The rectangle's origin is the <code>$x, $y</code> passed to <code>addUrl()</code> or <code>addLink()</code>, defaulting to <code>0</code>;
width and height extend up and to the right from there, so a 120 by 20 annotation added at
<code>72, 700</code> produces <code>[72, 700, 192, 720]</code> — <code>x, y</code> plus <code>x + width, y + height</code>. There is no default
width or height; both are required constructor arguments.</p>
<h2 id="border-appearance">Border Appearance<a class="anchor" href="#border-appearance" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>setBorderWidth()</code>, <code>setHRadius()</code>, <code>setVRadius()</code>, <code>setDashLength()</code> and <code>setDashGap()</code> all default
to <code>0</code>, and a <code>0</code> border width draws nothing — an annotation left at its defaults has no visible
outline. <code>Annotation\Link</code> inherits the same five setters, so a link between pages carries a border
exactly as a URL link does:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">TEXT</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code>/Border [6 6 2]
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>is what <code>setBorderWidth(2)-&gt;setHRadius(6)-&gt;setVRadius(6)</code> on a <code>Link</code> compiles to — the same
<code>[hRadius vRadius width]</code> shape a <code>Url</code> annotation produces. Setting a width is what makes either
one's rectangle appear:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Annotation\Url</span>;

<span class="text-var">$url</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Url</span>(<span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-num">40</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;https://example.com/a&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$url</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setBorderWidth</span>(<span class="text-num">3</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>setHRadius()</code> and <code>setVRadius()</code> write a horizontal and vertical corner radius into the same
border definition, but rounding the corners is left to the reader displaying the PDF — a border
rendered by this documentation's toolchain stays square-cornered at any radius, so treat the radii
as data a capable reader can act on rather than a guaranteed visual.</p>
<p><code>setDashLength()</code> and <code>setDashGap()</code> turn a solid border into a dashed one, and both have to be set
together — setting only one leaves the border solid. Set both, along with a border width, and the
rectangle renders as alternating dashes and gaps:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Annotation\Url</span>;

<span class="text-var">$url</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Url</span>(<span class="text-num">150</span>, <span class="text-num">40</span>, <span class="text-str">&#039;https://example.com/b&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$url</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setBorderWidth</span>(<span class="text-num">2</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setDashLength</span>(<span class="text-num">6</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">setDashGap</span>(<span class="text-num">3</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The compiled border definition writes the pair as <code>[dashGap dashLength]</code> — <code>[3 6]</code> for the call
above — so the gap comes first in the emitted array even though <code>setDashLength()</code> is called first in
the chain:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">TEXT</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code>/Border [0 0 2 [3 6]]
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>getBorderWidth()</code>, <code>getHRadius()</code>, <code>getVRadius()</code>, <code>getDashLength()</code> and <code>getDashGap()</code> read every
value back, in the order you set them rather than the order the compiled array writes them in.</p>
<p>Leaving every border setter at its default is the common case. Reach for <code>setBorderWidth()</code> when
the clickable area has nothing under it and needs its own visible edge.</p>
